// Auth models are generated in auth.prisma by `pnpm auth:schema`.
// This file retains deferred Payvoke domain drafts only. The minimal active
// App/AppCommand/AppCommandRevision/ChatThread/Quote/DeploymentPolicy
// definitions live in commerce.prisma; merge these drafts as features ship,
// do not uncomment duplicate definitions wholesale.
// Invocation/settlement journal definitions are active in payments.prisma.
// S01: API/provider; S02: x402/vault; S03: local MCP buyer client.
// Opaque IDs remain case-sensitive text. EVM addresses must be normalized to
// lowercase at the application boundary; hashes are full-width lowercase hex.
// Decimal(78, 0) stores atomic uint256 amounts, never floating-point USDC.
// Nonnegative/uint256 bounds, immutable published snapshots, state transitions,
// actor XOR rules and signature checks require transactional application logic
// and, when migrations are introduced, appropriate SQL CHECKs/triggers.
// Chain projections are not an independent source of spendable credit.
// No buyer private keys, external bearer/API tokens, or local MCP approvals
// are stored here. Better Auth owns its native session token/cookie storage.
// Encrypted authorization payloads require external key management.

